  2048                              <1> rawend:
  2049                              <1> RAWSIZE equ     (rawend-tstart+1FFh) & ~1FFh
  2050 00000DA0 00<rep 60h>         <1>         times   (-(rawend-tstart)) & 1FFh db 0
  2051                              <1> 
  2052                              <1> ; ---- the interpreter's variables, after the code (zero at the start) -------
  2053                              <1> ; They are in the zeros that pad the section to its FileAlignment, or past
  2054                              <1> ; them in the uninitialised part: within 127 bytes of `next` either way.
  2055                              <1>         absolute rawend
